<%#
  A row's actions, collapsed into a menu.

    render "shared/essentials/row_actions", label: "distribution #{d.id}", items: [
      {label: "Print", path: print_distribution_path(d), icon: "bi-printer"},
      {label: "Edit",  path: edit_distribution_path(d),  icon: "bi-pencil"},
      {label: "Reclaim", path: distribution_path(d), icon: "bi-arrow-counterclockwise",
       method: :delete, tone: :danger, confirm: "Are you sure?"}
    ]

  Locals:
    label    required; names the row, so a screen reader hears "More actions for distribution 24"
             rather than "button" once per row
    items    required; each {label:, path:, icon:, method:, confirm:, tone:, disabled:, reason:}
    primary  optional; rendered as a visible button beside the trigger
    size     optional; `:sm` (28px, the default, for a table row) or `:md` (38px, to stand beside
             the page header's own buttons)

  **It is also the page header's overflow.** A record page's Edit and Delete go here rather than
  beside the primary: the header allows three actions and a menu counts as one, and a destructive
  action should never inherit the last slot, which belongs to the primary. `menu_button` is the
  wrong component for that -- it collapses a single item back to a button, and it is named after
  its contents, which works for two exports and not for "edit and delete". See design.md.

  Five labelled buttons made the actions column 331px on /distributions -- the second-widest
  column in the table, wider than Total items, Total value and Status together. Collapsed it is
  70px. Carbon ships this as `OverflowMenu`, Salesforce calls it row-level actions, and GitHub,
  Drive, Gmail, Notion, Linear and Stripe all end a row with a kebab. See design.md.

  `primary` is omitted where the row's first cell already links to the record: a visible "View"
  beside a linked ID is two controls with one destination.

  The items themselves are `shared/essentials/menu_items`, shared with `menu_button`, so what a
  menu item is has one definition rather than two that drift.

  The disclosure pattern, not the ARIA menu pattern: a popover of links moved through with Tab.
  `popover_controller` already gives Escape, focus back to the trigger, `aria-expanded` and
  click-outside; it does not do arrow-key movement, and promising `role="menu"` without that is
  worse than not promising it.
%>
<div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap">
  <%= primary if defined?(primary) && primary %>

  <%# `popover-fixed-value`: this menu is inside `.table-scroll`, which clips on both axes, so the
      panel is placed against the viewport instead. Without it the last row's menu is cut off by
      the bottom of the table. %>
  <%#
    `aria-controls` on the trigger, and an id on the panel. The ARIA menu-button pattern recommends
    it, and it is what makes the panel findable now that `popover_controller` moves it to `<body>`
    while it is open -- the audits and the spec helper had been reaching it through the DOM, which
    a portal breaks. Random rather than derived from the label, because two rows in one table can
    share a name and two elements cannot share an id.
  %>
  <% panel_id = "row-actions-#{SecureRandom.hex(4)}" %>
  <div class="relative" data-controller="popover" data-popover-fixed-value="true">
    <button type="button"
            <%# `size-7` in a row, not the 38px control height: a row action is `sm` sized everywhere
        else in the app, and a 38px trigger made every distribution row 10px taller. 28px still
        clears WCAG 2.5.8's 24x24 floor. In a page header it is 2.375rem -- 38px, the control
        height design.md fixes -- so it stands level with the buttons beside it rather than 10px
        short of them. Not `size-10`, which is 40 and was 2px proud of them. %>
            class="inline-flex <%= (local_assigns[:size].to_s == "md") ? "size-[2.375rem] border border-slate-300 bg-white" : "size-7" %> items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-slate-500 transition-colors hover:bg-slate-100 hover:text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brand-600"
            aria-haspopup="true"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-label="More actions for <%= label %>"
            aria-controls="<%= panel_id %>"
            data-popover-target="trigger"
            data-action="click->popover#toggle">
      <i class="bi-three-dots-vertical" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>

    <%# `role="menu"` with `role="menuitem"` children, and the popover controller now implements the
        arrow-key movement that role promises -- see popover_controller. The overlay audit requires
        a popover panel to declare what it is. %>
    <div class="absolute right-0 z-30 w-56 py-1 <%= EssentialsUiHelper::POPOVER_SURFACE_CLASSES %>"
         id="<%= panel_id %>"
         hidden
         role="menu"
         data-popover-target="panel">
      <%= render "shared/essentials/menu_items", items: items %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
